            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0325" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002 Manchuria/254: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-09-04T15:00:00+08:00">September 4, 1932—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 4—5 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1063. Legation’s 1060, September 3, 3 p.m. Following from Mukden: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“September 3, noon. Referring to my telegram of September 2, 5 p.m.,
                            Japanese consular authorities undertake to do their utmost to ensure
                            Talbot’s safety in railway concession but assume no responsibility for
                            his protection outside that area. In their opinion the situation is the
                            result of his continued presence and can be satisfactorily liquidated by
                            his departure. I am informing Talbot to this effect.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
